{
  "id": "dishabituation",
  "term": "dishabituation",
  "definition": "Dishabituation is the return of an orienting response after it has weakened through repeated exposure, triggered by changing to a new or novel stimulus. In this context, it means that a response reduced by habituation becomes re-established when something different is presented.",
